  "adaptations_and_remaining_gaps": [
    "The inline pointer slot contains None/null rather than native myPtr==myStorage. Getter addresses match storage behavior after relocation, but raw pointer-slot bytes, self-referential field observation and direct binary ABI interchange are not equivalent. The measured size/offset closure must not be read as whole-layout byte equivalence.",
    "Public generic LocalArray<T,N> remains SmallVec-backed with its existing layout and allocation differences. This specialized private owner does not implement or claim all LocalArray resizing, views, nontrivial payload callbacks, raw mutable fields or generic template instantiations.",
    "Common allocator ownership uses the existing Rust header before each heap payload. Requested i32 payload bytes are correct, but native global allocator callbacks, total physical heap footprint, external memory-manager modes and OOM exception details are not proved equivalent.",
    "The node request row compares native Allocate arguments with actual Rust arena consumption at those8-aligned concrete sizes; it does not expose a new Rust allocator subclass callback or establish arbitrary alignment/request equivalence.",
    "Coordinates are initialized to zero before filling, where some native inline bytes may be indeterminate. Only initialized logical coordinates and retained live heap ownership are exposed safely; arbitrary reads beyond the logical range and native uninitialized-byte observations are unclaimed.",
    "Existing standalone Cell discard/Drop-unwind and allocator metadata adaptations remain as previously documented. This receipt closes three measured concrete size/head-offset gaps, adds no automatic global API credit, and leaves compiler/body equivalence and full API/test parity open."
  ]
